@startuml Project Authentication
title Authentication
note top
Summary: Shows patient and staff code sign-in, admin PIN sign-in, and the current versus planned email delivery paths.
end note

actor Patient
actor "Doctor / Admin" as Doctor
actor Staff
participant "Booking App" as App
participant "Auth and Access" as Auth
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Email Preview / Provider" as Email

== Patient code sign-in ==
Patient -> App: Enter email and request one-time code
App -> Auth: Request patient code
Auth -> DB: Save expiring code request
alt Localhost test mode
    App --> Patient: Prompt for requested test code (0000)
else Email delivery is connected in a future release
    Auth --> Email: Planned login-code delivery
    Email --> Patient: Planned one-time code delivery
end
Patient -> App: Submit code
App -> Auth: Verify code and register patient if new
Auth -> DB: Check code, register patient if new, start session
DB --> App: Patient session

== Staff code sign-in ==
Staff -> App: Enter email and request code
App -> Auth: Verify active staff account and issue code
Auth -> DB: Save expiring code request
alt Localhost test mode
    App --> Staff: Prompt for requested test code (0000)
else Email delivery is connected in a future release
    Auth --> Email: Planned staff login-code delivery
    Email --> Staff: Planned one-time code delivery
end
Staff -> App: Submit code
App -> Auth: Verify staff code (staff must already exist)
Auth -> DB: Check active staff access and create session

== Doctor/admin PIN sign-in ==
Doctor -> App: Sign in with email and PIN
App -> Auth: Verify admin PIN and access
Auth -> DB: Check account, lockout and session
DB --> App: Admin session
@enduml
